speech_text:
The motion teeth/kerstens (
The room,
heard the deliberation,
noting that at the European Patent Office in Rijswijk and Munich there has been targeted attacks on trade union members and a very high workload for some time;
Furthermore, finding that the EOB as an international organization does not fall under national labor law;
Whereas such violations of the standards of the International Labor Organization, certainly if they take place on Dutch territory, are unacceptable;
The government requests to consult with other Member States of the EOB about measures to prevent these abuses and how to regulate the legal gap in these labor conflicts, following the now -agreed process of the "Social Audit", with other Member States,
And proceeds to the order of the day.
